Library fines.

A loan has a title (text) and days late (a whole number).

The fine for a loan (a loan) is money:
0 if its days late is at most 0,
5 if its days late times 0.25 is more than 5,
otherwise its days late times 0.25.

The fines of some loans (a list of loans) is money:
the sum of the fine for the loan for each loan in the loans.

Suppose dune is a loan with title "Dune" and days late 4.
Suppose emma is a loan with title "Emma" and days late 60.
Suppose ulysses is a loan with title "Ulysses" and days late 0.
For example, the fine for dune is 1.
For example, the fine for emma is 5.
For example, the fine for ulysses is 0.
For example, the fines of a list of dune, emma and ulysses is 6.
